  "notes": "The Rabin terminal has a long cream passenger hall, red steel inspection canopies and a white entry fascia. Across the paved crossing, Jordan’s two sculpted arches with a gold crown stand before blue-roofed checkpoint halls. The reconstruction represents the two passenger terminals and visible border gateways. Window divisions, roof details, signage ornament and service equipment are interpreted from public imagery. Standard terrain controls the grades of the buildings and gate islands. The original mapped roadway and surrounding land use remain part of the native map.",
